This solution incorporates curated excerpts from authoritative, permissively
licensed public datasets for demonstration and benchmarking:

1. Contract Understanding Atticus Dataset (CUAD) v1
   Source: The Atticus Project (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4595826)
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Usage: Curated excerpts of real SEC EDGAR Exhibit 10 commercial contracts
   and expert clause annotations (Change of Control, Anti-Assignment, License
   Grant, IP Ownership) used in packs/legal_ma_clause_graph/.

2. U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) EDGAR Public Filings
   Source: https://www.sec.gov/edgar (Form 10-K, Form SD Conflict Minerals
   Reports, Exhibit 21.1 Subsidiaries, Exhibit 10 Material Contracts)
   License: U.S. Government Public Domain.

3. U.S. Department of the Treasury — Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC)
   Source: https://www.treasury.gov/ofac/downloads/ (SDN, ALT, ADD lists)
   License: U.S. Government Public Domain.

4. U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) — Mineral Commodity Summaries
   Source: https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/ (USGS National Minerals
   Information Center)
   License: U.S. Government Public Domain.

5. Global Legal Entity Identifier Foundation (GLEIF) — LEI Level 1 & 2 Data
   Source: https://api.gleif.org/
   License: Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0 Public Domain).

Any hypothetical disruption scenarios, modeled SKU revenue splits, redacted
contract deal schedules, or fictional bank loan applicants added solely to
demonstrate end-to-end what-if contagion simulations are explicitly labeled
with data_origin="MODELED_BRIDGE" in both storage tables and UI badges.
